- Host establishes framebuffer range in memory (or receives allocation info from module).
- Host calls exported functions (init/draw) or polls flags, then reads memory slice and blits to canvas (ImageData.data in JS) or to an OS window surface.

5) Command buffer format (example)
If you prefer batching:

Command entry (u32 opcode, followed by operands packed as u32/u16/u8):
- Opcodes:
  - 0x01: CLEAR color (u32 rgba)
  - 0x02: FILL_RECT x y w h color
  - 0x03: COPY_SRC src_offset dest_offset size
  - 0x04: DRAW_SUBIMAGE src_offset sx sy sw sh dx dy
- The module writes commands sequentially into a ring buffer; a write pointer and read pointer are kept in memory or supplied by host. Host parses and executes on present or frame boundary.

