- For deterministic image generation you can also implement a tiny interpreter limited to a predictable subset (no floating point, no threads, no non-deterministic host calls). This reduces scope drastically.

7) Performance & implementation tips
- Prefer memory writes over per-pixel host calls.
- Use typed bulk operations when possible: wasm memory.fill, memory.copy (Bulk Memory proposal) — faster for large fills/copies.
- Pack color as u32 and store via aligned stores where possible to reduce per-byte operations.
- If you use SIMD (if supported and deterministic), you can accelerate blits inside wasm.
- Use double buffering (module writes to back buffer, host swaps on present).
- Avoid runtime allocations in module where host can provide buffers.

